arXiv:2509.11298v1 [cs.LG] 14 Sep 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="p1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\keepXColumns</span>
</div>
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">
<span id="id1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:357.7pt;">
<span id="id1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Madhava Gaikwad</span>
<span id="id1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Microsoft</span>
<span id="id1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="id1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mgaikwad@microsoft.com</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">We present Opal, an operator view of reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF).
Objectives are expressed as ladders of two primitives on a base utility: <em id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">additive</em> penalties
and <em id="abstract1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multiplicative</em> pairwise weights. We show a simple reduction law with <em id="abstract1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">if-and-only-if</em> conditions:
such ladders collapse to a normal form on pairwise margins when the reference is fixed, penalties are additive,
and weights are independent of intermediate margins. When these assumptions do not hold (reference shift,
non-additive gates, score-dependent weights), finite examples witness non-reducibility.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.2" class="ltx_p">Building on this view, we introduce GKPO (Generalized Kernel Preference Object),
a canonical schema that many RLHF methods can be expressed in and, when reducible,
mapped back from. GKPO provides a standard JSON serialization, canonicalization and hashing rules,
and explicit flags with finite witnesses when assumptions fail.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.3" class="ltx_p">As illustrations, we show worked GKPO examples for DPO, RRHF, and ORPO,
cross-method conversions via GKPO (where assumptions permit), and minimal stress tests (SHIFT/GATE/SCORE)
that surface non-reducibility. We also release a small Python reference library implementing the GKPO schema,
canonical hashing, and adapters for DPO and RRHF.</p>
  
</div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="p2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_top">
<tr id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:24.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF) has become a central ingredient in aligning large language models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christiano et al., 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022a</a>)</cite>.
Meanwhile, the space of objectives has fragmented into a “zoo”: PPO-RLHF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christiano et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, direct preference optimization (DPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, ranking-based methods (RRHF) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuan et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, offset-regularized objectives (ORPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, variance-shaping approaches (KTO/GRPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ethayarajh et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and divergence-modified variants (e.g., f-DPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, among others.
This proliferation raises a basic question: are two objectives fundamentally different, or merely algebraic rearrangements of related operators?</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We propose Opal, an operator algebra for RLHF.
In Opal, an objective is a <em id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ladder</em> built from two primitives on a base score <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>: (i) <em id="S1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">additive</em> penalties that shift scores, and (ii) <em id="S1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multiplicative</em> pairwise weights that scale margins.
We show a reduction law: such ladders collapse to a single normal form on pairwise margins, <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math>, if and only if three assumptions hold—(a) the reference is fixed, (b) penalties combine additively, and (c) weights are independent of intermediate margins.
When an assumption fails (reference shift, non-additive gating, or score-dependent weights), one can exhibit small, concrete witnesses where no normal form matches all pairs.
This perspective helps explain equivalences (e.g., PPO-RM <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> DPO under a fixed reference) and clarifies when proposals necessarily differ in decisions or losses.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Building on the algebra, we introduce GKPO (Generalized Kernel Preference Object), a canonical, method-agnostic schema for RLHF.
Any objective can be represented as a GKPO instance; inside the reducible class, GKPO canonicalizes to Opal’s normal form (with a deterministic hash for provenance), and outside it records explicit failure flags with finite witnesses (reference shift / gate / score dependence).
GKPO functions as an interchange: method <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\to</annotation></semantics></math> GKPO <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> method <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> preserves margins (up to positive scaling) whenever the reduction conditions hold.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contributions.</h4>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Operator view for RLHF. We formalize objectives as ladders of penalties and weights and give an if-and-only-if reduction law yielding a normal form on margins under simple assumptions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Non-reducibility witnesses. We provide finite witnesses for three failure modes—reference shift, non-additive gates, and score-dependent weights—indicating when no <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> can match all pairs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GKPO schema. We design a compact JSON schema with canonicalization and hashing rules that (i) collect reducible ladders to a normal form and (ii) surface irreducible assumptions with flags and witnesses.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Demonstrations. We include worked GKPO examples (DPO, RRHF, ORPO), cross-method conversions via GKPO where applicable, and small stress tests (SHIFT/GATE/SCORE) that reveal non-reducibility.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reference implementation. A lightweight Python library (see <a href="https://github.com/krimler/opal-gkpo" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">github.com/krimler/opal-gkpo</a>; <span id="S1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gkpo.py</span> with <span id="S1.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adapters/dpo.py</span>, <span id="S1.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adapters/rrhf.py</span>) implements the schema, deterministic hashing, adapters, and basic probes to support reproducibility.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, Opal is intended as a <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">simple organizing view</em> for reasoning about RLHF objectives and GKPO as a <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">practical interchange representation</em> for unifying, comparing, and reproducing method configurations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Background and Operator Algebra</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setting and notation.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each prompt <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with candidate set <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, let a <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">base score</em>
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\{(x,y)\}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\{(x,y)\}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> induce pairwise differences
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta u(x;y^{+},y^{-})\coloneqq u(x,y^{+})-u(x,y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta u(x;y^{+},y^{-})\coloneqq u(x,y^{+})-u(x,y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>.
An RLHF objective on pairs <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> is evaluated via a scalar <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">margin</em>
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and a strictly increasing <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">link</em> <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> inside a scalar loss <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\,\ell\bigl(g(\beta\,M(x;y^{+},y^{-}))\bigr),\qquad\beta&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\,\ell\bigl(g(\beta\,M(x;y^{+},y^{-}))\bigr),\qquad\beta&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{+}\succ y^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{+}\succ y^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> when the decision induced by <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> prefers <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Primitive operators and ladders</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We model objectives as <em id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ladders</em> of operators acting on a base pair <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,1)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,1)\xrightarrow{O_{1}}\cdots\xrightarrow{O_{m}}(f,W)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.1389em">→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">O</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub></mover><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">O</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">m</mi></msub></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,1)\xrightarrow{O_{1}}\cdots\xrightarrow{O_{m}}(f,W),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is a transformed score and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a pairwise weight. We also allow a
<em id="S2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reference</em> adjustment <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}:\{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}:\{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The canonical margin of a ladder <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\;=\;\bigl(\Delta f(x;y^{+},y^{-})-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\bigr)\cdot W(x;y^{+},y^{-})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\;=\;\bigl(\Delta f(x;y^{+},y^{-})-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\bigr)\cdot W(x;y^{+},y^{-}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Definition 1</span> (Primitive operators).</h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\{(x,y)\}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\{(x,y)\}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega:\{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}\to\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega:\{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}\to\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ul id="S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Additive penalty </span><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}[\lambda,\phi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}[\lambda,\phi]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:
 </span><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,W)\mapsto(\,f-\lambda\phi,\;W\,)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,W)\mapsto(\,f-\lambda\phi,\;W\,)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Multiplicative weight </span><math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}[\omega]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}[\omega]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:
 </span><math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,W)\mapsto(\,f,\;W\cdot\omega\,)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,W)\mapsto(\,f,\;W\cdot\omega\,)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reference adjust </span><math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}[\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}[\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:
 leaves </span><math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,W)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> unchanged but contributes the subtraction
</span><math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to the margin.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A <em id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">ladder</em> is a finite sequence <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}\in\mathcal{A}\cup\mathcal{M}\cup\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}\in\mathcal{A}\cup\mathcal{M}\cup\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Commutation/associativity)<span id="Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Additive penalties commute and associate under sum on <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>;
multiplicative weights commute and associate under product on <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, any ladder induces <em id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">collected</em> representatives</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\;=\;u-\sum_{i\in I}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i},\qquad W\;=\;\prod_{j\in J}\omega_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\;=\;u-\sum_{i\in I}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i},\qquad W\;=\;\prod_{j\in J}\omega_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>) indexes additive (resp. multiplicative) operators in <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Margin semantics and the reducible class <math id="S2.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Definition 2</span> (Margin semantics).</h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,W,\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,W,\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math> from a ladder <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}\;=\;(\Delta f-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot W,\qquad\text{and decisions are }\operatorname{sign}(M_{L})\ \text{(or via $g,\ell$).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and decisions are </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(or via </mtext><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">).</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}\;=\;(\Delta f-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot W,\qquad\text{and decisions are }\operatorname{sign}(M_{L})\ \text{(or via $g,\ell$).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Two ladders <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,L^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,L^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are <em id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">margin-equivalent</em> if <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}\equiv M_{L^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}\equiv M_{L^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Definition 3</span> (Reducible ladders and normal form).</h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of ladders whose operators satisfy:
(i) <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">fixed</em> (does not vary across prompts pairs),
(ii) penalties are <em id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">additive</em> (no data-dependent gates on <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>),
(iii) weights are <em id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">score-independent</em> (do not depend on intermediate <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f</annotation></semantics></math>).
A <em id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">normal form</em> representative of <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a pair <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}\;=\;u-\sum_{i\in I}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i},\qquad w^{\ast}\;=\;\prod_{j\in J}\omega_{j},\qquad M_{L}\equiv(\Delta f^{\ast}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\,w^{\ast}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}\;=\;u-\sum_{i\in I}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i},\qquad w^{\ast}\;=\;\prod_{j\in J}\omega_{j},\qquad M_{L}\equiv(\Delta f^{\ast}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\,w^{\ast}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Closure)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, additive penalties are closed under sum on <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and multiplicative
weights under product on <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore any ladder <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a collected
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> computed in one pass over <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{1},\ldots,O_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{1},\ldots,O_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Definition 4</span> (Equivalence up to positive scaling).</h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Write <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,w)\sim(\tilde{f},\tilde{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,w)\sim(\tilde{f},\tilde{w})</annotation></semantics></math> if there exists <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant:
<math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta\tilde{f}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\tilde{w}=(\Delta f-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta\tilde{f}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\tilde{w}=(\Delta f-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})w</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Loss–link invariance)<span id="Thmremark2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing, equal margins imply equal decisions and order-consistent
losses <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(g(\beta M))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(g(\beta M))</annotation></semantics></math>; thus <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> preserves optimization and evaluation up to a
positive rescaling of <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Normal form as a homomorphism</h3>

<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Definition 5</span> (Free monoid and homomorphism).</h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> be the free monoid of operator strings on the alphabet
<math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\cup\mathcal{M}\cup\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\cup\mathcal{M}\cup\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (concatenation). Define
<math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H:\mathcal{L}^{\ast}\to\mathbb{R}^{\{(x,y)\}}\times\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}^{\{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}}\times\mathbb{R}^{\{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H:\mathcal{L}^{\ast}\to\mathbb{R}^{\{(x,y)\}}\times\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}^{\{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}}\times\mathbb{R}^{\{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}}</annotation></semantics></math>
by <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(L)=(f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(L)=(f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math> with collection rules of <a href="#Thmremark1" title="Remark 1 (Commutation/associativity). ‣ 2.1 Primitive operators and ladders ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Remark</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Then concatenation maps to sum/product on <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> and addition on references.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Ladder <math id="Thmproposition1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> normal form (algebraic view))<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Restricted to <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is a surjective monoid homomorphism modulo the scaling
equivalence <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> of <a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Equivalence up to positive scaling). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Hence every <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to a unique
<math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> up to positive scaling (cf. <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Uniqueness up to positive scaling). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.4 </span>Failure modes (outside <math id="S2.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will show explicit finite witnesses that violate reducibility:</p>
<ul id="S2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reference shift (<a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Reference shift). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>): <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> varies across prompts <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>
no single <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> preserves decisions on all pairs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Non-additive gates (<a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Gated penalties). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>): gated penalties cannot be represented by a nonnegative
additive surrogate agreeing on all items.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Score-dependent weights (<a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>): if <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\psi(\Delta f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\psi(\Delta f)</annotation></semantics></math> with nonconstant <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>,
operator order can flip decisions; no score-independent <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> reproduces all outcomes.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Algorithmic note (one-pass collection).</h4>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a ladder <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, initialize <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\leftarrow(u,1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\leftarrow(u,1,0)</annotation></semantics></math> and
for <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}=\begin{cases}\mathcal{A}[\lambda,\phi]&amp;\Rightarrow\ f^{\ast}\leftarrow f^{\ast}-\lambda\phi,\\
\mathcal{M}[\omega]&amp;\Rightarrow\ w^{\ast}\leftarrow w^{\ast}\cdot\omega,\\
\mathcal{R}[\rho]&amp;\Rightarrow\ \Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}\leftarrow\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}+\rho.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}=\begin{cases}\mathcal{A}[\lambda,\phi]&amp;\Rightarrow\ f^{\ast}\leftarrow f^{\ast}-\lambda\phi,\\
\mathcal{M}[\omega]&amp;\Rightarrow\ w^{\ast}\leftarrow w^{\ast}\cdot\omega,\\
\mathcal{R}[\rho]&amp;\Rightarrow\ \Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}\leftarrow\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}+\rho.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This runs in <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(m)</annotation></semantics></math> and yields the normal form when <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, it produces a candidate together with
flags indicating which assumptions failed (to be formalized by GKPO in <a href="#S4" title="4 GKPO: A Canonical Interchange Schema ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Theoretical Results</h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Theorem 1</span> (Reduction).</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any ladder <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}\in\mathcal{A}\cup\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}\in\mathcal{A}\cup\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and a fixed <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where penalties are additive and weights are independent of intermediate margins,
there exists <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\;=\;\bigl[\Delta f^{\ast}(x;y^{+},y^{-})-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\bigr]\cdot w^{\ast}(x,y^{+},y^{-})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\;=\;\bigl[\Delta f^{\ast}(x;y^{+},y^{-})-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\bigr]\cdot w^{\ast}(x,y^{+},y^{-}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Conversely, if any assumption fails (reference shift, non-additive gates, or score-dependent weights),
there exist finite witnesses where no <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> matches <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> on all pairs.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11298v1/opal_reduction_diagram.png" id="S3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:132/198;" width="132" height="198" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Ladder to normal form: additive penalties collect into f*; multiplicative weights collect into w*; reference adjustments accumulate separately.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof sketch.</h6>
<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Sufficiency: by <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Closure). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, collect additive terms into <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
and multiplicatives into <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>; margin equality holds pointwise.
Necessity: the finite witnesses are given by <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Reference shift). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorems</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Gated penalties). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Theorem 2</span> (Reference shift).</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> varies across prompts, there is no single <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> preserving decisions on all pairs.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Witness.</h6>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Two prompts with equal raw gap <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}&gt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}&gt;d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}&lt;-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}&lt;-d</annotation></semantics></math>
flip the margin sign; a single fixed reference cannot match both.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Theorem 3</span> (Gated penalties).</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi=\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}\,\mathbf{1}\{\phi_{1}=0\}\phi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi=\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}\,\mathbf{1}\{\phi_{1}=0\}\phi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exists a finite set of items on which no nonnegative additive surrogate matches decisions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Witness.</h6>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})=(1,10)\Rightarrow\Phi=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})=(1,10)\Rightarrow\Phi=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text"> (gate off) and <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)\Rightarrow\Phi=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)\Rightarrow\Phi=1</annotation></semantics></math> (gate on).
Matching both enforces <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}^{\prime}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}^{\prime}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}^{\prime}=-9&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}^{\prime}=-9&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, contradicting nonnegativity.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Theorem 4</span> (Score-dependent weights).</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\psi(\Delta f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\psi(\Delta f)</annotation></semantics></math> with nonconstant <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, operator order can flip decisions;
no score-independent <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> reproduces all outcomes.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Witness.</h6>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(y^{+})=0.4,\ u(y^{-})=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y^{+})=0.4,\ u(y^{-})=0.0</annotation></semantics></math>; an additive penalty shifts <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.8</annotation></semantics></math> (post-gap <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.4</annotation></semantics></math>).
Take <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\Delta)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\Delta)=2</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, else <math id="S3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Weight<math id="S3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!\to</annotation></semantics></math>penalty yields factor <math id="S3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>; penalty<math id="S3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!\to</annotation></semantics></math>weight yields <math id="S3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>; decisions differ.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Loss–link invariance)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing and two operators yield equal margins <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>,
then decisions and any loss <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(g(\beta M))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(g(\beta M))</annotation></semantics></math> coincide (up to a monotone transform).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Uniqueness up to positive scaling)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If two reduced representatives <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{f},\tilde{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{f},\tilde{w})</annotation></semantics></math>
induce identical margins for all pairs, then <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\,c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\,c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> s.t. <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f^{\ast})w^{\ast}=(\Delta\tilde{f})\tilde{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f^{\ast})w^{\ast}=(\Delta\tilde{f})\tilde{w}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text"> pointwise;
set <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=(\Delta\tilde{f})/(\Delta f^{\ast})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=(\Delta\tilde{f})/(\Delta f^{\ast})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> wherever <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f^{\ast}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f^{\ast}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and extend by continuity.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Gradient equivalence inside <math id="Thmproposition2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}\,\ell(g(\beta M_{\theta}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}\,\ell(g(\beta M_{\theta}))</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}=(\Delta f_{\theta}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}=(\Delta f_{\theta}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot W</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> independent of intermediate <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}\equiv M^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}\equiv M^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical under the ladder and its normal form <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>GKPO: A Canonical Interchange Schema</h2>

<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Object.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Generalized Kernel Preference Object</em> (GKPO) encodes, for pairwise data <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{GKPO}\;=\;\bigl(f,\;w,\;\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}},\;g,\;\ell,\;\beta,\;\Pi,\;\Omega,\;\mathsf{meta}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>GKPO</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝗆𝖾𝗍𝖺</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{GKPO}\;=\;\bigl(f,\;w,\;\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}},\;g,\;\ell,\;\beta,\;\Pi,\;\Omega,\;\mathsf{meta}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\!(x,y)\!\mapsto\!\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.108em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\!(x,y)\!\mapsto\!\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the score (typically <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\log\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\log\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>),
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w:\!(x,y^{+},y^{-})\!\mapsto\!\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.108em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w:\!(x,y^{+},y^{-})\!\mapsto\!\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> a pairwise weight,
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> a reference adjustment, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> a strictly increasing link, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> a scalar loss,
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> a temperature, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi=\{(\lambda_{i},\phi_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi=\{(\lambda_{i},\phi_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math> additive penalties, and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> dataset-level operators.
Its <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">canonical margin</em> is</p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\;=\;(\Delta f-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot w,\qquad\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}\,\ell\!\big(g(\beta M)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.247em;" width="0.247em"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\;=\;(\Delta f-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot w,\qquad\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}\,\ell\!\big(g(\beta M)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Inside the reducible class <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Reducible ladders and normal form). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> folds into <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> and multiplicatives into <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the Opal normal form; outside <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> the object still represents the method but carries explicit failure flags with finite witnesses.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Schema (keys and types)</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a compact, implementation-ready key set; full JSON Schema appears in Appendix.</p><pre id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{
  "version": "gkpo-1.0",
  "score":     { "type": "logpi" | "logit" | "custom", "custom_name": "..." },
  "weight":    { "form": "constant"|"product"|"score_dependent"|"custom",
                 "constant": 1.0, "factors": ["..."], "score_fn": "psi_name" },
  "reference": { "form": "fixed_zero"|"fixed_scalar"|"per_dataset"|"per_prompt"|"custom",
                 "value": 0.0 },
  "link": "identity"|"logistic"|"tanh"|"hinge"|"custom",
  "loss": "logistic"|"bce"|"hinge"|"mse"|"custom",
  "beta": 1.0,
  "penalties":  [ { "name": "phi_i", "lambda": 0.123 }, ... ],
  "dataset_ops":{ "group_weights": ["..."], "group_penalties": ["..."],
                  "composition": "dataset_then_policy"|"policy_then_dataset" },
  "provenance": { "opal_hash": "SHA256(...)", "method": "DPO|RRHF|...",
                  "citations": ["bibkey1","bibkey2"], "notes": "..." },
  "reducibility": { "inside_R": true|false,
                    "reasons": ["reference_shift"|"score_dependent_weight"|"non_additive_gate"],
                    "witness": { ... } }
}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Canonicalization and hashing</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(C1) Collection. Compute <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> (one pass; <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Closure). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
(C2) Scale fixing. Choose <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{median}_{\text{probe}}(|\Delta f^{\ast}|)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>median</mi><mtext>probe</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{median}_{\text{probe}}(|\Delta f^{\ast}|)=1</annotation></semantics></math> and apply the invariance
<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\beta)\mapsto(c\,\Delta f^{\ast},c^{-1}w^{\ast},c\,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\beta)\mapsto(c\,\Delta f^{\ast},c^{-1}w^{\ast},c\,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Equivalence up to positive scaling). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Uniqueness up to positive scaling). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
(C3) Deterministic serialization. Emit UTF-8 JSON with: keys sorted, arrays lexicographically sorted
(by <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">name</span> for penalties, by value for lists), numeric rounding at <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>.
(C4) Opal hash. Define <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">opal_hash</span> <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> SHA-256 of (C3). The hash is invariant across equivalent representatives
and flips with any operator, coefficient, reference, or ordering change.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Mapping existing methods (adapters)</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DPO.   <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">score=logpi</span>, <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">weight.constant=1</span>, <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reference=fixed_scalar</span>,
<span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">link=identity</span>, <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">loss=logistic</span>, <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">penalties=[]</span>. Reducible; normal form equals config.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PPO-RM <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> DPO.   KL anchor additive; with fixed reference, reduces to DPO (<a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Reduction). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, Loss–link <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Loss–link invariance). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RRHF.   Ranking penalties appear in <span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">penalties</span>; collected into <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>; reducible if other assumptions hold.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ORPO.   Reducible when reference fixed and penalties linear; else flag <span id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reference_shift</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">KTO/GRPO.   If variance shaping realizes as pairwise multiplicatives independent of <math id="S4.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f</annotation></semantics></math>, set <span id="S4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">weight.form="product"</span>;
otherwise use <span id="S4.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"score_dependent"</span> and flag.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Divergence-modified (e.g., f-DPO/VAR/EGPO).   Reference varies across prompts or weights depend on <math id="S4.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f</annotation></semantics></math>:
set <span id="S4.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reference.form="per_prompt"</span> and/or <span id="S4.I1.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">weight.form="score_dependent"</span> and attach witness.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Dataset-level operators.   Group weights/penalties recorded in <span id="S4.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dataset_ops</span>; if additive/multiplicative,
composition collapses inside <math id="S4.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (dataset<math id="S4.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\circ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∘</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\circ</annotation></semantics></math>policy = policy<math id="S4.I1.i7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\circ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∘</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\circ</annotation></semantics></math>dataset under collection).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Non-reducibility flags and witnesses</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GKPO records failures of the assumptions of <a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Reducible ladders and normal form). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> using <span id="S4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reducibility</span>:</p>
<table id="S4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.SS4.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Reason</td>
<td id="S4.SS4.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Minimal witness (encoded in <span id="S4.SS4.p1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">witness</span>)</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.SS4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.SS4.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S4.SS4.p1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reference_shift</span></td>
<td id="S4.SS4.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Two prompts with same <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> but opposite-signed <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> (sign flip).</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.SS4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.SS4.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S4.SS4.p1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">non_additive_gate</span></td>
<td id="S4.SS4.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Pairs <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})=(1,10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})=(1,10)</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> force negative surrogate weight.</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.SS4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.SS4.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S4.SS4.p1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">score_dependent_weight</span></td>
<td id="S4.SS4.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Interleavings yield different <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f</annotation></semantics></math> crosses 0.</td></tr>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Example (reference shift):</p><pre id="S4.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
"reducibility": {
  "inside_R": false,
  "reasons": ["reference_shift"],
  "witness": { "delta_ref_prompt1": +0.5, "delta_ref_prompt2": -0.5, "raw_gap": 0.2 }
}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Practical notes</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluation order. GKPO always evaluates <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(g(\beta M))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(g(\beta M))</annotation></semantics></math>; strictly increasing <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> preserves decisions and order-consistent losses (<a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Loss–link invariance). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
Gradients. When <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of intermediate <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, gradients under a ladder and under its normal form coincide (<a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Gradient equivalence inside ℛ). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
Artifacts. We release a minimal Python reference library (<span id="S4.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gkpo.py</span> with <span id="S4.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adapters/dpo.py</span>, <span id="S4.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adapters/rrhf.py</span>)
implementing the schema, canonical hashing, adapters, and stress probes to support reproducibility.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Demonstrations (Worked Examples)</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We replace large-scale evaluations with compact, copyable demonstrations that exercise Opal’s algebra
and GKPO’s interchange. Each example uses concrete numbers so margins and decisions can be checked by hand.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Worked GKPO Examples (Toy Pairs)</h3>

<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Toy dataset.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider one prompt <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with two candidates <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> and a base score <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\log\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\log\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"></td>
<td id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x,y^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x,y^{+})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x,y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x,y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">values</td>
<td id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,-1.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,-1.20</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,-1.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.70</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,-1.70</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta u=u(x,y^{+})-u(x,y^{-})=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta u=u(x,y^{+})-u(x,y^{-})=0.50</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DPO as GKPO.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With a fixed reference <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=0.10</annotation></semantics></math>, constant weight <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=1</annotation></semantics></math>, identity link and logistic loss,
the margin and loss are</p>
<table id="S5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{DPO}}=(\Delta u-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot 1=0.40,\qquad\ell_{\mathrm{logistic}}(M)=\log\!\bigl(1+e^{-M}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>logistic</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{DPO}}=(\Delta u-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot 1=0.40,\qquad\ell_{\mathrm{logistic}}(M)=\log\!\bigl(1+e^{-M}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A minimal GKPO instance is:</p><pre id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{
  "version": "gkpo-1.0",
  "score":     { "type": "logpi" },
  "weight":    { "form": "constant", "constant": 1.0 },
  "reference": { "form": "fixed_scalar", "value": 0.10 },
  "link": "identity", "loss": "logistic", "beta": 1.0,
  "penalties": [], "dataset_ops": { "composition": "dataset_then_policy" },
  "provenance": { "method": "DPO", "citations": ["rafailov2023direct"] },
  "reducibility": { "inside_R": true, "reasons": [], "witness": {} }
}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RRHF as GKPO (additive penalties).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose the method adds two ranking penalties to the base score,
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=u-\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}-\lambda_{2}\phi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=u-\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}-\lambda_{2}\phi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2})=(0.50,0.10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2})=(0.50,0.10)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{1}(x,y^{+})-\phi_{1}(x,y^{-})=0.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{1}(x,y^{+})-\phi_{1}(x,y^{-})=0.20</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{2}(x,y^{+})-\phi_{2}(x,y^{-})=-0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{2}(x,y^{+})-\phi_{2}(x,y^{-})=-0.10</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f\;=\;\Delta u-0.50(0.20)-0.10(-0.10)\;=\;0.50-0.10+0.01\;=\;0.41,\quad M_{\mathrm{RRHF}}=(\Delta f-0)\cdot 1=0.41." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.50</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 0.50</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0.41</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>RRHF</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.41</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f\;=\;\Delta u-0.50(0.20)-0.10(-0.10)\;=\;0.50-0.10+0.01\;=\;0.41,\quad M_{\mathrm{RRHF}}=(\Delta f-0)\cdot 1=0.41.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The GKPO instance differs only in <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">penalties</span>:</p><pre id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
"penalties": [
  { "name": "rank_margin_1", "lambda": 0.50 },
  { "name": "rank_margin_2", "lambda": 0.10 }
]
</pre>
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Inside <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, GKPO’s collection step folds these into <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>; the margin is unchanged.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ORPO as GKPO (fixed vs. shifting reference).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If ORPO uses a fixed offset (dataset-constant <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>), it is reducible and
identical in form to DPO (possibly with extra penalties). If the offset varies across prompts,
GKPO records <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reference.form="per_prompt"</span> and sets a failure flag; see <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Stress Tests: SHIFT / GATE / SCORE ‣ 5 Demonstrations (Worked Examples) ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Conversions (Method <math id="S5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\to</annotation></semantics></math> GKPO <math id="S5.SS2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> Method <math id="S5.SS2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<section id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RRHF <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> GKPO <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> DPO (when reducible).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the toy RRHF above, if (i) reference is fixed, (ii) penalties are additive, and (iii) weights are
score-independent, then the margin <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\Delta f)\cdot 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\Delta f)\cdot 1</annotation></semantics></math> equals the DPO margin with
<math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, RRHF reduces to DPO by identity mapping on <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.
Formally, pick any <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and apply the scaling invariance
<math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f,w,\beta)\mapsto(c\,\Delta f,c^{-1}w,c\,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f,w,\beta)\mapsto(c\,\Delta f,c^{-1}w,c\,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. <a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Equivalence up to positive scaling). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definitions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Uniqueness up to positive scaling). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)
to match DPO’s preferred <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> without changing decisions or order-consistent losses.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PPO-RM <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> GKPO <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> DPO.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\log\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\log\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and fixed reference, the KL anchor is additive in <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>;
Bradley–Terry yields a logistic loss in <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\Delta u-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\Delta u-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Reduction). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Loss–link invariance (<a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Loss–link invariance). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), PPO-RM and DPO
define the same margins up to positive scaling; GKPO makes this equivalence explicit by
folding anchor terms into <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> and keeping <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Score-dependent variants (no conversion).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If a method implements <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\psi(\Delta f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\psi(\Delta f)</annotation></semantics></math> with nonconstant <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, then GKPO sets
<span id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">weight.form="score_dependent"</span> and blocks conversion to any score-independent target
(e.g., DPO) because margins depend on operator order (<a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Stress Tests: SHIFT / GATE / SCORE</h3>

<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SHIFT (reference shift).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two prompts have identical raw gap <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=0.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=0.20</annotation></semantics></math> but opposite reference adjustments:
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}=+0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}=+0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}=-0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}=-0.50</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(1)}=(0.20-0.50)\cdot 1=-0.30,\qquad M^{(2)}=(0.20+0.50)\cdot 1=+0.70." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0.20</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0.20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(1)}=(0.20-0.50)\cdot 1=-0.30,\qquad M^{(2)}=(0.20+0.50)\cdot 1=+0.70.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Any single fixed <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot match both signs; GKPO sets
<span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">inside_R=false</span>, <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reasons=["reference_shift"]</span> and records the witness:</p><pre id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
"witness": { "raw_gap": 0.20, "delta_ref_prompt1": +0.50, "delta_ref_prompt2": -0.50 }
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GATE (non-additive gating).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Take <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi=\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}\,\mathbf{1}\{\phi_{1}=0\}\phi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi=\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}\,\mathbf{1}\{\phi_{1}=0\}\phi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and two items:
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})=(1,10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})=(1,10)</annotation></semantics></math> (gate off) and <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> (gate on). Both give <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Matching both with a nonnegative additive surrogate enforces <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\prime}_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\prime}_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\prime}_{1}=-9&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\prime}_{1}=-9&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
a contradiction (<a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Gated penalties). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). GKPO can store <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">non_additive_gate</span> with these points.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SCORE (score-dependent weights).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(y^{+})=0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y^{+})=0.40</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(y^{-})=0.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y^{-})=0.00</annotation></semantics></math>. An additive penalty shifts <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.80</annotation></semantics></math>, giving post-gap <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.40</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\Delta)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\Delta)=2</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> else <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{weight}\!\to\!\text{penalty: }(0.40)\cdot\tfrac{1}{2}=0.20\;&gt;\;0,\quad\text{penalty}\!\to\!\text{weight: }(-0.40)\cdot 2=-0.80\;&lt;\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>weight</mtext><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>penalty: </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.40</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mo lspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>penalty</mtext><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>weight: </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.40</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.80</mn><mo lspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{weight}\!\to\!\text{penalty: }(0.40)\cdot\tfrac{1}{2}=0.20\;&gt;\;0,\quad\text{penalty}\!\to\!\text{weight: }(-0.40)\cdot 2=-0.80\;&lt;\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so decisions differ by operator order (<a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). GKPO sets
<span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">weight.form="score_dependent"</span> and flags <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">score_dependent_weight</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reporting.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each test we report the sign of <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, Kendall-<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> on toy permutations, and the GKPO <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">opal_hash</span>.
Because hashing is computed from a canonical JSON (sorted keys, rounded numerics), any change to operators,
coefficients, or references deterministically alters the hash (cf. <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Canonicalization and hashing ‣ 4 GKPO: A Canonical Interchange Schema ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Operational check.</span> Appendix <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Operational Validation of the Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a> corroborates these demonstrations: matched-normal-form PPO–RM vs. DPO are empirically indistinguishable (Table <a href="#A8.T3" title="In Controls and reporting. ‣ Appendix H Operational Validation of the Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), while introducing a prompt-varying reference produces the predicted behavioral differences (Table <a href="#A8.T4" title="In Controls and reporting. ‣ Appendix H Operational Validation of the Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Method Taxonomy under Opal</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We summarize representative RLHF objectives under Opal’s operator view.
A method is <em id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Reducible (Yes)</em> if its operators are additive on <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, multiplicative on <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, and use a fixed reference (<a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Reducible ladders and normal form). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>);
<em id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Depends</em> if reducible under explicit assumptions (e.g., fixed reference, linear penalties);
<em id="S6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">No</em> when any non-reducibility theorem applies (<a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Reference shift). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorems</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Gated penalties). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T1" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Opal taxonomy summary. ”Yes” means reducible to the normal form (f*, w*); ”Depends” requires stated assumptions; ”No” violates reducibility (reference shift, non-additive gate, score-dependent weight). Refs: PPO–RLHF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christiano et al., 2017</a>)</cite>; DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2023</a>)</cite>; RRHF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuan et al., 2023</a>)</cite>; ORPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al., 2024</a>)</cite>; KTO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ethayarajh et al., 2024</a>)</cite>; GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>; f-DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al., 2024</a>)</cite>; RLAIF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2023</a>)</cite>; Constitutional AI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022b</a>)</cite>; HH pipelines <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Askell et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S6.T1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">(a) Assumptions for reducibility by method

<span id="S6.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Method</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">In R?</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Assumptions for reducibility</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">PPO–RLHF (RM)</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Yes</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Fixed reference; KL folded additively</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">DPO</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Yes</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Standard configuration</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">RRHF</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Yes</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Linear/additive penalties; fixed reference</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">ORPO</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Depends</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Fixed offset; linear penalties</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">KTO / GRPO</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Depends</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Variance shaping realized as score-independent multiplicatives</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">f<span id="S6.T1.2.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>DPO</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">Depends/No</span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">If reference varies across prompts, not reducible</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T1.2.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math>-style PO / VAR / EGPO</span>
