<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Full Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Closure (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Closure). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="Thmlemmax1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemmax1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lemma</span></span><span id="Thmlemmax1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Closure)<span id="Thmlemmax1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemmax1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemmax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within <math id="Thmlemmax1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, additive penalties are closed under sum on <math id="Thmlemmax1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and multiplicative
weights under product on <math id="Thmlemmax1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore any ladder <math id="Thmlemmax1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a collected
<math id="Thmlemmax1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> computed in one pass over <math id="Thmlemmax1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{1},\ldots,O_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{1},\ldots,O_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each additive operator <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}[\lambda,\phi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}[\lambda,\phi]</annotation></semantics></math> applies <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,W)\mapsto(f-\lambda\phi,W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,W)\mapsto(f-\lambda\phi,W)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By commutativity/associativity of addition, composing any finite set of such operators yields
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged. Likewise, each multiplicative operator
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}[\omega]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}[\omega]</annotation></semantics></math> applies <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,W)\mapsto(f,W\cdot\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,W)\mapsto(f,W\cdot\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>; by commutativity/associativity of
multiplication over <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>, composing finitely many gives <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged.
Interleavings commute on <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,W)</annotation></semantics></math> because addends act only on <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and factors only on <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus a single left-to-right pass computes
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Reduction Theorem (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Reduction). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="Thmtheoremx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheoremx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theorem</span></span><span id="Thmtheoremx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Reduction)<span id="Thmtheoremx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheoremx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any ladder <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}\in\mathcal{A}\cup\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}\in\mathcal{A}\cup\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and a fixed <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where penalties are additive and weights are independent of intermediate margins,
there exists <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}(x;y^{+},y^{-})=\bigl[\Delta f^{\ast}(x;y^{+},y^{-})-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\bigr]\cdot w^{\ast}(x,y^{+},y^{-})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}(x;y^{+},y^{-})=\bigl[\Delta f^{\ast}(x;y^{+},y^{-})-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}(x;y^{+},y^{-})\bigr]\cdot w^{\ast}(x,y^{+},y^{-}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Conversely, if any assumption fails (reference shift, non-additive gates, or score-dependent weights),
there exist finite witnesses where no <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> matches <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> on all pairs.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Sufficiency.</em><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"> By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Closure). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, collect addends/factors to obtain
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed
(across prompts/pairs) and weights do not depend on intermediate <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f</annotation></semantics></math>, the composed margin equals
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f^{\ast}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f^{\ast}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Necessity.</em><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"> If reference shift occurs, choose two prompts with the same raw gap <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
but <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}&gt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}&gt;d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}&lt;-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}&lt;-d</annotation></semantics></math>; margins flip sign, so no fixed reference
can match both decisions (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Reference shift). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). If gated penalties appear, the pairs
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})=(1,10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})=(1,10)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> force any nonnegative additive surrogate to take <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}^{\prime}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}^{\prime}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
(contradiction; Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Gated penalties). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). If score-dependent weights appear,
interleavings around a sign change of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f</annotation></semantics></math> yield different decisions; no score-independent <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>
can match both (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). In each case a finite witness set suffices.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Non-reducibility Theorems (Theorems <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Reference shift). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>–<a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)</h3>

<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reference shift (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Reference shift). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</h4>

<div id="Thmtheoremx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheoremx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theorem</span></span><span id="Thmtheoremx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Reference shift)<span id="Thmtheoremx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheoremx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheoremx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Thmtheoremx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> varies across prompts, there is no single <math id="Thmtheoremx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> preserving decisions on all pairs.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let two prompts have the same <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f=d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f=d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}&gt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}&gt;d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}&lt;-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}&lt;-d</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(1)}=(d-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)})&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(1)}=(d-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)})&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(2)}=(d-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(2)}=(d-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (for any positive <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>).
A fixed <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot realize both signs simultaneously; hence no single normal form matches both.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gated penalties (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Gated penalties). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</h4>

<div id="Thmtheoremx3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheoremx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theorem</span></span><span id="Thmtheoremx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Gated penalties)<span id="Thmtheoremx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheoremx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheoremx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmtheoremx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi=\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}\,\mathbf{1}\{\phi_{1}=0\}\phi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi=\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}\,\mathbf{1}\{\phi_{1}=0\}\phi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a finite set of items on which
no nonnegative additive surrogate matches decisions.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider items with <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})\in\{(1,10),(0,1)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})\in\{(1,10),(0,1)\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(1,10)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(1,10)=1</annotation></semantics></math> (gate off) and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(0,1)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(0,1)=1</annotation></semantics></math> (gate on).
Any additive surrogate <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\prime}=\lambda_{1}^{\prime}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}^{\prime}\phi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\prime}=\lambda_{1}^{\prime}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}^{\prime}\phi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> that agrees on these points must satisfy
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}^{\prime}+10\lambda_{2}^{\prime}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}^{\prime}+10\lambda_{2}^{\prime}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}^{\prime}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}^{\prime}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}^{\prime}=-9&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}^{\prime}=-9&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. If nonnegativity is required (as in many penalty designs),
this is impossible. A standard separation or Farkas’ lemma argument yields a finite certificate in the general case.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Score-dependent weights (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</h4>

<div id="Thmtheoremx4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheoremx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theorem</span></span><span id="Thmtheoremx4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Score-dependent weights)<span id="Thmtheoremx4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheoremx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheoremx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Thmtheoremx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\psi(\Delta f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\psi(\Delta f)</annotation></semantics></math> with nonconstant <math id="Thmtheoremx4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, operator order can flip decisions; no score-independent <math id="Thmtheoremx4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> reproduces all outcomes.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(y^{+})=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y^{+})=0.4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(y^{-})=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y^{-})=0.0</annotation></semantics></math>. An additive penalty shifts <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, so the post-gap is <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.4</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\Delta)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\Delta)=2</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, else <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{weight}\!\to\!\text{penalty: }(0.4)\cdot\tfrac{1}{2}=0.2&gt;0,\quad\text{penalty}\!\to\!\text{weight: }(-0.4)\cdot 2=-0.8&lt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>weight</mtext><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>penalty: </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>penalty</mtext><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>weight: </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{weight}\!\to\!\text{penalty: }(0.4)\cdot\tfrac{1}{2}=0.2&gt;0,\quad\text{penalty}\!\to\!\text{weight: }(-0.4)\cdot 2=-0.8&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Decisions differ by interleaving, but any score-independent <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> would give the same decision under both orders, a contradiction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Loss–link invariance (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Loss–link invariance). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="Thmlemmax2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemmax2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lemma</span></span><span id="Thmlemmax2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Loss–link invariance)<span id="Thmlemmax2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemmax2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemmax2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Thmlemmax2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing and two operators yield equal margins <math id="Thmlemmax2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, then decisions and any loss <math id="Thmlemmax2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(g(\beta M))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(g(\beta M))</annotation></semantics></math> coincide
(up to a monotone transform).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Decision invariance: <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{sign}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{sign}(M)</annotation></semantics></math> is preserved under strictly increasing <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and positive <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Loss invariance: If two margins <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1}\equiv M_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1}\equiv M_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\beta M_{1})=g(\beta M_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\beta M_{1})=g(\beta M_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise.
Any scalar loss <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> applied to equal arguments is equal. If instead two links <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},g_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},g_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are both strictly increasing,
there exists a strictly increasing <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=g_{2}\circ g_{1}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=g_{2}\circ g_{1}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> on the common range; losses related by <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}(\cdot)=\ell_{1}(h^{-1}(\cdot))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}(\cdot)=\ell_{1}(h^{-1}(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math>
are order-equivalent.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Uniqueness up to positive scaling (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Uniqueness up to positive scaling). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="Thmlemmax3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemmax3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lemma</span></span><span id="Thmlemmax3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Uniqueness)<span id="Thmlemmax3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemmax3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemmax3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If two reduced representatives <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{f},\tilde{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{f},\tilde{w})</annotation></semantics></math> induce identical margins for all pairs,
then <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\,c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\,c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">From <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f^{\ast})w^{\ast}=(\Delta\tilde{f})\tilde{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f^{\ast})w^{\ast}=(\Delta\tilde{f})\tilde{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast},\tilde{w}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast},\tilde{w}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> we get
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{\Delta\tilde{f}}{\Delta f^{\ast}}=\dfrac{w^{\ast}}{\tilde{w}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{\Delta\tilde{f}}{\Delta f^{\ast}}=\dfrac{w^{\ast}}{\tilde{w}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> wherever <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f^{\ast}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f^{\ast}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The left-hand side depends only on <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast},\tilde{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast},\tilde{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, the right-hand side only on <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast},\tilde{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast},\tilde{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the ratio varied across pairs, we could pick two pairs with distinct ratios <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\neq c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\neq c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; then no positive <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously on both pairs, contradicting equality of margins.
Thus the ratio is constant <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on the support of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\tilde{f}=c\,\Delta f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>
(for zero gaps extend by continuity or define <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> arbitrarily as the limit). Then necessarily <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}=c^{-1}w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Gradient equivalence (Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Gradient equivalence inside ℛ). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="Thmpropositionx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmpropositionx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proposition</span></span><span id="Thmpropositionx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Gradient equivalence inside <math id="Thmpropositionx1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmpropositionx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmpropositionx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmpropositionx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmpropositionx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}\,\ell(g(\beta M_{\theta}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}\,\ell(g(\beta M_{\theta}))</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmpropositionx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}=(\Delta f_{\theta}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}=(\Delta f_{\theta}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot W</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="Thmpropositionx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> independent of intermediate <math id="Thmpropositionx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Thmpropositionx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{L}\equiv M^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{L}\equiv M^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="Thmpropositionx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical under the ladder and its normal form <math id="Thmpropositionx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By chain rule,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\ell^{\prime}\!\big(g(\beta M_{\theta})\big)\,g^{\prime}(\beta M_{\theta})\,\beta\cdot\nabla_{\theta}M_{\theta}\right],\qquad\nabla_{\theta}M_{\theta}=(\nabla_{\theta}\Delta f_{\theta})\cdot W," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\ell^{\prime}\!\big(g(\beta M_{\theta})\big)\,g^{\prime}(\beta M_{\theta})\,\beta\cdot\nabla_{\theta}M_{\theta}\right],\qquad\nabla_{\theta}M_{\theta}=(\nabla_{\theta}\Delta f_{\theta})\cdot W,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent of intermediate <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the ladder and its collected normal form, <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> enter only through the product
<math id="A1.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f_{\theta})\cdot W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f_{\theta})\cdot W</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the same by margin equivalence. Thus the integrands coincide pointwise,
hence so do the expectations and gradients.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Extended GKPO Schema</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Design goals.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(1) Represent any pairwise RLHF objective with explicit operators,
(2) canonicalize reducible ladders to a normal form,
(3) emit deterministic hashes for provenance,
(4) attach explicit non-reducibility flags and finite witnesses when assumptions fail.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>JSON Schema (informal, compact)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><pre id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{
  "version": "gkpo-1.0",
  "score": {
    "type": "logpi" | "logit" | "custom",
    "custom_name": string?         // e.g., "rm_logit"
  },
  "weight": {
    "form": "constant" | "product" | "score_dependent" | "custom",
    "constant": number?,           // used iff form == "constant"
    "factors": [string]?,          // names of multiplicative factors (product)
    "score_fn": string?            // e.g., "psi_softplus"; implies score_dependent
  },
  "reference": {
    "form": "fixed_zero" | "fixed_scalar" | "per_dataset" | "per_prompt" | "custom",
    "value": number?               // used iff form in {fixed_zero, fixed_scalar}
  },
  "link": "identity" | "logistic" | "tanh" | "hinge" | "custom",
  "loss": "logistic" | "bce" | "hinge" | "mse" | "custom",
  "beta": number,                  // temperature &gt; 0
  "penalties": [
    { "name": string, "lambda": number, "meta": { "gate": bool? } }  // optional gate flag
  ],
  "dataset_ops": {
    "group_weights": [string],     // names of dataset-level multiplicative ops
    "group_penalties": [string],   // names of dataset-level additive ops
    "composition": "dataset_then_policy" | "policy_then_dataset"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "opal_hash": string,           // SHA-256 over deterministic JSON (see below)
    "method": string,              // e.g., "DPO", "RRHF"
    "citations": [string],         // bib keys
    "notes": string
  },
  "reducibility": {
    "inside_R": boolean,
    "reasons": [ "reference_shift" | "score_dependent_weight" | "non_additive_gate" ],
    "witness": object              // minimal numeric witness payload
  }
}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Canonicalization &amp; deterministic hashing</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fix a canonical representative (up to positive scaling; cf. <a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Equivalence up to positive scaling). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definitions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Uniqueness up to positive scaling). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and a stable byte encoding.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">C1: Collection.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fold penalties into <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and multiplicatives into <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>
(<a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Closure). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">C2: Scale fixing (optional, recommended).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Choose <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{median}_{\text{probe}}(|\Delta f^{\ast}|)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>median</mi><mtext>probe</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{median}_{\text{probe}}(|\Delta f^{\ast}|)=1</annotation></semantics></math> and apply
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\beta)\mapsto(c\,\Delta f^{\ast},c^{-1}w^{\ast},c\,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\beta)\mapsto(c\,\Delta f^{\ast},c^{-1}w^{\ast},c\,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, preserving margins
(<a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Equivalence up to positive scaling). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definitions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Uniqueness up to positive scaling). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">C3: Deterministic JSON.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sort all <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">object keys</em> lexicographically; sort arrays by:
penalties by <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">name</span>, factor lists lexicographically, dataset-op lists lexicographically.
Round all floating-point numeric fields to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> (decimal, half-even acceptable).
Serialize with UTF-8 JSON, compact separators (comma, colon), no trailing spaces.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">C4: Opal hash.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">opal_hash</span> as the hex SHA-256 of the C3 byte string.
Any change to operators, coefficients, reference form/value, lists, or ordering deterministically changes the hash;
equivalent representations inside <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> share the same hash after C1–C3.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Pseudocode</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><pre id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
function CANONICALIZE_AND_HASH(gkpo):
  f_star, w_star &lt;- collect(gkpo.penalties, gkpo.weight)     // C1
  if want_scale_fix:
    c &lt;- 1 / median_abs_delta(f_star)                        // probe set
    (f_star, w_star, beta) &lt;- (c*f_star, w_star/c, c*gkpo.beta) // C2
  blob &lt;- deterministic_json({
    version, score, link, loss, beta,
    weight:=canonical_weight(w_star), reference,
    penalties:=sorted_penalties(), dataset_ops:=sorted_ops(),
    reducibility, provenance:=provenance_without_hash
  }, round=1e-6)                                             // C3
  h &lt;- sha256_hex(blob)                                      // C4
  return (f_star, w_star, h)
</pre>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Validation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Schema correctness: (i) all required keys present, (ii) enum values respected, (iii) number fields parseable after rounding,
(iv) arrays sorted as specified. Canonicalization is idempotent: re-serializing a canonical object yields identical bytes and hash.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Worked Examples</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide copyable GKPO snippets with explicit numbers so margins and decisions can be verified.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Example A: DPO baseline (fixed reference)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Base scores: <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x,y^{+})=-1.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x,y^{+})=-1.10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x,y^{-})=-1.60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.60</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x,y^{-})=-1.60</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta u=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta u=0.50</annotation></semantics></math>.
Set <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=0.15</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{DPO}}=(0.50-0.15)\cdot 1=0.35&gt;0\;\Rightarrow\;y^{+}\succ y^{-}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0.50</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.35</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{DPO}}=(0.50-0.15)\cdot 1=0.35&gt;0\;\Rightarrow\;y^{+}\succ y^{-}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table><pre id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{
  "version":"gkpo-1.0",
  "score":{"type":"logpi"},
  "weight":{"form":"constant","constant":1.0},
  "reference":{"form":"fixed_scalar","value":0.15},
  "link":"identity","loss":"logistic","beta":1.0,
  "penalties":[],
  "dataset_ops":{"group_weights":[],"group_penalties":[],"composition":"dataset_then_policy"},
  "provenance":{"method":"DPO","citations":["rafailov2023direct"]},
  "reducibility":{"inside_R":true,"reasons":[],"witness":{}}
}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Example B: RRHF penalties fold into <math id="A3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2})=(0.4,0.2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2})=(0.4,0.2)</annotation></semantics></math> with margin deltas
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\phi_{1}=0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\phi_{1}=0.10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\phi_{2}=-0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\phi_{2}=-0.05</annotation></semantics></math>. With the same <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta u=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta u=0.50</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f=\Delta u-0.4\cdot 0.10-0.2\cdot(-0.05)=0.50-0.04+0.01=0.47,\quad M=(\Delta f-0)\cdot 1=0.47&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.50</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.04</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.47</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.47</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f=\Delta u-0.4\cdot 0.10-0.2\cdot(-0.05)=0.50-0.04+0.01=0.47,\quad M=(\Delta f-0)\cdot 1=0.47&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table><pre id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
"penalties":[{"name":"rank_margin_1","lambda":0.4},
             {"name":"rank_margin_2","lambda":0.2}]
</pre>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">After collection, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> substitutes <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> in the canonical margin; <span id="A3.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">opal_hash</span> is stable across
penalty reordering due to sorted arrays and rounding (§<a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Extended GKPO Schema ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Example C: ORPO with prompt-varying offset (reference shift)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prompt 1: <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta u=0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta u=0.30</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}=+0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(1)}=+0.40</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(1)}=-0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(1)}=-0.10</annotation></semantics></math>;
Prompt 2: <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta u=0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta u=0.30</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}=-0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{(2)}=-0.10</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(2)}=+0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(2)}=+0.40</annotation></semantics></math>.
No single fixed <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> matches both signs (<a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Reference shift). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
GKPO (diff from DPO in <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reference.form</span> and witness):</p><pre id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
"reference":{"form":"per_prompt"},
"reducibility":{"inside_R":false,
  "reasons":["reference_shift"],
  "witness":{"raw_gap":0.30,"delta_ref_prompt1":+0.40,"delta_ref_prompt2":-0.10}}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Example D: Score-dependent weights (SCORE)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Base: <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta u=0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta u=0.40</annotation></semantics></math>; additive penalty later may flip sign. Take
<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\Delta)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\Delta)=2</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, else <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
If weight then penalty: <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0.40\cdot(1/2)=0.20&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.40</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0.40\cdot(1/2)=0.20&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If penalty then weight with post-gap <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.40</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M=-0.40\cdot 2=-0.80&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.40</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.80</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=-0.40\cdot 2=-0.80&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
GKPO:</p><pre id="A3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
"weight":{"form":"score_dependent","score_fn":"psi_piecewise"},
"reducibility":{"inside_R":false,"reasons":["score_dependent_weight"],"witness":{}}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Example E: Non-additive gate (GATE)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Items: <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})\in\{(1,10),(0,1)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})\in\{(1,10),(0,1)\}</annotation></semantics></math>; gated <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi=\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}1\{\phi_{1}=0\}\phi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi=\lambda_{1}\phi_{1}+\lambda_{2}1\{\phi_{1}=0\}\phi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
yields <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi=1</annotation></semantics></math> on both items. Any nonnegative additive surrogate forces <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}^{\prime}=-9&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}^{\prime}=-9&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Gated penalties). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
GKPO (record gate metadata and witness points):</p><pre id="A3.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
"penalties":[{"name":"phi1","lambda":1.0,"meta":{"gate":false}},
             {"name":"phi2_gate_on_phi1_zero","lambda":1.0,"meta":{"gate":true}}],
"reducibility":{"inside_R":false,"reasons":["non_additive_gate"],
  "witness":{"phi_pairs":[[1,10],[0,1]],"phi_value_equal":1.0}}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6 </span>Example F: Conversion with scale invariance</h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose a method yields margin <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\Delta f)\cdot 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\Delta f)\cdot 0.5</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{median}(|\Delta f|)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>median</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{median}(|\Delta f|)=2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choosing <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1/\mathrm{median}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>median</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1/\mathrm{median}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f^{\prime},w^{\prime},\beta^{\prime})=(0.5\Delta f,1.0,0.5\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f^{\prime},w^{\prime},\beta^{\prime})=(0.5\Delta f,1.0,0.5\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Decisions and order-consistent losses are unchanged (<a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Equivalence up to positive scaling). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definitions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Loss–link invariance). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>); the canonical hash uses the scaled triple.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical check.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each example, a reference implementation (<span id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gkpo.py</span>) reproduces the canonical JSON,
hash, and reducibility flags as reported here (Appendix code artifact).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Normal Form Gallery</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We list canonical representatives <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> (up to positive scaling; <a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Equivalence up to positive scaling). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definitions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Uniqueness up to positive scaling). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)
for representative methods as encoded by GKPO.
Where reducibility assumptions fail, we record the primary flag and give the closest admissible <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> for comparison.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Inside <math id="A4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (reducible)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all entries below, the canonical margin is <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\Delta f^{\ast}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\Delta f^{\ast}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\cdot w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DPO.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}=u,\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed scalar}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>fixed scalar</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u,\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed scalar}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GKPO diff from template: <code id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">"reference":{"form":"fixed_scalar","value":c}</code>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PPO–RLHF (RM) <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> DPO.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\lambda\,\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\quad\text{(penalty folded additively)},\qquad w^{\ast}=1,\qquad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>(penalty folded additively)</mtext><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>fixed</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\lambda\,\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\quad\text{(penalty folded additively)},\qquad w^{\ast}=1,\qquad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Loss–link invariance + <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Reduction). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> imply DPO-equivalent margins.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RRHF (linear ranking penalties).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\,\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>fixed</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\,\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GKPO: <code id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">"penalties":[{"name":...,"lambda":...},...]</code>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ORPO (fixed offset; linear penalties).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\,\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed scalar}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>fixed scalar</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\,\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed scalar}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If penalties are linear and the offset is dataset-constant, margins reduce to DPO form.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">KTO/GRPO (score-independent variance shaping).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\,\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\quad\text{(none depends on $\Delta f$)},\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>(none depends on </mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>fixed</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\,\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=\prod_{j}\omega_{j}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\quad\text{(none depends on $\Delta f$)},\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{fixed}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GKPO: <code id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">"weight":{"form":"product","factors":[...] }</code>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Depends (conditional reducibility) or Outside <math id="A4.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When an assumption fails, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{\ast},w^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> is not guaranteed to reproduce decisions. GKPO records flags/witnesses.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ORPO with prompt-varying offset (reference shift).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Flag: }\texttt{reference\_shift},\qquad f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{per-prompt}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Flag: </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">reference_shift</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>per-prompt</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Flag: }\texttt{reference\_shift},\qquad f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{per-prompt}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No single fixed <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> matches all pairs (<a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Reference shift). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Divergence-modified variants (e.g., f-DPO, VAR/EGPO cases) with prompt-dependent anchors.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Flag: }\texttt{reference\_shift},\qquad f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{k}\lambda_{k}\phi_{k},\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{per-prompt}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Flag: </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">reference_shift</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>per-prompt</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Flag: }\texttt{reference\_shift},\qquad f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{k}\lambda_{k}\phi_{k},\quad w^{\ast}=1,\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}=\text{per-prompt}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Score-dependent weighting.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Flag: }\texttt{score\_dependent\_weight},\qquad f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=\psi(\Delta f)\ \text{(nonconstant)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Flag: </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">score_dependent_weight</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>(nonconstant)</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Flag: }\texttt{score\_dependent\_weight},\qquad f^{\ast}=u-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\phi_{i},\quad w^{\ast}=\psi(\Delta f)\ \text{(nonconstant)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Order can flip decisions; no score-independent <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> reproduces all outcomes (<a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Score-dependent weights). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gated penalties.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Flag: }\texttt{non\_additive\_gate},\qquad f^{\ast}\ \text{undefined as a nonnegative additive surrogate on the witness set}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Flag: </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">non_additive_gate</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mtext>undefined as a nonnegative additive surrogate on the witness set</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Flag: }\texttt{non\_additive\_gate},\qquad f^{\ast}\ \text{undefined as a nonnegative additive surrogate on the witness set}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finite witness forces a negative coefficient in any additive surrogate (<a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Gated penalties). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Copyable GKPO snippets (canonical form)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All snippets assume identity link and logistic loss; extend as needed.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DPO (fixed scalar reference).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><pre id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{"score":{"type":"logpi"},
 "weight":{"form":"constant","constant":1.0},
 "reference":{"form":"fixed_scalar","value":0.10},
 "link":"identity","loss":"logistic","beta":1.0,
 "penalties":[], "reducibility":{"inside_R":true,"reasons":[],"witness":{}}}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RRHF (two linear penalties).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><pre id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{"score":{"type":"logpi"},
 "weight":{"form":"constant","constant":1.0},
 "reference":{"form":"fixed_zero","value":0.0},
 "link":"identity","loss":"logistic","beta":1.0,
 "penalties":[
   {"name":"rank_margin_1","lambda":0.50},
   {"name":"rank_margin_2","lambda":0.10}],
 "reducibility":{"inside_R":true,"reasons":[],"witness":{}}}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">KTO/GRPO (score-independent product weight).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><pre id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{"score":{"type":"logpi"},
 "weight":{"form":"product","factors":["var_floor","clip_snr"]},
 "reference":{"form":"fixed_zero","value":0.0},
 "link":"identity","loss":"logistic","beta":1.0,
 "penalties":[],
 "reducibility":{"inside_R":true,"reasons":[],"witness":{}}}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ORPO with reference shift (flagged).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><pre id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{"score":{"type":"logpi"},
 "weight":{"form":"constant","constant":1.0},
 "reference":{"form":"per_prompt"},
 "link":"identity","loss":"logistic","beta":1.0,
 "penalties":[],
 "reducibility":{"inside_R":false,
   "reasons":["reference_shift"],
   "witness":{"raw_gap":0.20,"delta_ref_prompt1":+0.50,"delta_ref_prompt2":-0.50}}}
</pre>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Scale note (one-liner)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All forms are defined up to <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\beta)\mapsto(c\,\Delta f^{\ast},c^{-1}w^{\ast},c\,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta f^{\ast},w^{\ast},\beta)\mapsto(c\,\Delta f^{\ast},c^{-1}w^{\ast},c\,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
which preserves decisions and order-consistent losses (<a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Equivalence up to positive scaling). ‣ 2.2 Margin semantics and the reducible class ℛ ‣ 2 Background and Operator Algebra ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definitions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Loss–link invariance). ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
Our canonicalization fixes scale via <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{median}(|\Delta f^{\ast}|)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>median</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{median}(|\Delta f^{\ast}|)=1</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Extended GKPO Schema ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Reproducibility Statement</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a minimal, self-contained artifact to reproduce all demonstrations and tables:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reference library: <span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gkpo.py</span> implementing the GKPO schema, canonicalization, deterministic hashing, and reducibility flags.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adapters: <span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adapters/dpo.py</span>, <span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adapters/rrhf.py</span> (plus a simple ORPO constructor) that round-trip configurations where reducible.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stress probes: <span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SHIFT/GATE/SCORE</span> routines producing the finite witnesses used in the paper.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Copyable JSON: all GKPO snippets in the paper/appendix can be run verbatim; the artifact prints the canonical JSON and the <span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">opal_hash</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tests: <span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tests/test_roundtrip.py</span> covering DPO round-trip, reference-shift flag, score-dependent-weight flag, and deterministic hashing.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">How to reproduce. (i) Run <span id="A5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">python gkpo.py</span> to see hashes and flags for the toy configurations in Sec. <a href="#S5" title="5 Demonstrations (Worked Examples) ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>;
(ii) run <span id="A5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pytest</span> to verify round-trips and flags; (iii) paste the JSON snippets from App. <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Additional Worked Examples ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> to confirm identical <span id="A5.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">opal_hash</span>.
All random choices are fixed (toy numbers are constants), and the canonicalization uses median-based scale fixing as specified in App. <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Extended GKPO Schema ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.
No large models or private datasets are required.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Ethics Statement</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our work proposes a formalism (Opal) and a schema (GKPO) for representing RLHF objectives;
it does not require training or deploying large models.
Nevertheless, RLHF research raises important considerations:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Human data and privacy. When GKPO captures objectives derived from human annotations (e.g., preference logs),
practitioners should ensure compliance with data-use agreements and privacy norms. Our artifact uses only synthetic examples.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fairness <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, culture <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">AlKhamissi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and safety <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Operator choices (penalties, weights, references) can encode social preferences.
GKPO improves transparency by explicitly serializing these choices (and flags when assumptions fail),
but does not guarantee value alignment; we encourage reporting of GKPO diffs for fairness/safety interventions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Misuse risks. Standardizing operators can make it easier to compose objectives that prioritize utility over safety.
We mitigate by (i) requiring explicit <span id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reducibility</span> flags and finite witnesses, (ii) encouraging publication of GKPO artifacts alongside results,
and (iii) documenting limitations (Sec. <a href="#S8" title="8 Discussion and Broader Impact ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environmental impact.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our demonstrations are toy; no large-scale training is needed.
We advocate publishing GKPO artifacts to reduce redundant large-scale experiments when methods are algebraically equivalent in margins.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Appendix F: A Brief History of RLHF Methods</h2>

<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Early pipelines and RLHF.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PPO-RLHF with preference data and reward modeling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christiano et al., 2017</a>)</cite> became foundational,
with subsequent alignment pipelines and best practices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Askell et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Direct preference objectives.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2023</a>)</cite> reframed pairwise likelihood ratios into a logistic objective
(with fixed reference), inspiring follow-ons and clarifications.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ranking and offsets.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RRHF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuan et al., 2023</a>)</cite> cast ranking heuristics as additive margin penalties; ORPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al., 2024</a>)</cite>
introduced offset-regularized optimization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variance shaping and weighting.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">KTO/GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ethayarajh et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> emphasized variance shaping; some variants can be represented
as multiplicative, score-independent weights, others not (Sec. <a href="#S6" title="6 Method Taxonomy under Opal ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Divergence-modified and hybrid objectives.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Methods that alter anchors/divergences or introduce learned, score-dependent weights can cross the boundary
of reducibility; Opal identifies these boundaries and provides explicit flags and witnesses (Sec. <a href="#S5" title="5 Demonstrations (Worked Examples) ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Human feedback alternatives.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RLAIF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and Constitutional AI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022b</a>)</cite> explored alternative data
and constraint sources, often composable as dataset-level operators in Opal when additive/multiplicative.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Copyable table.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A compact taxonomy table appears in the main text (Table <a href="#S6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 6 Method Taxonomy under Opal ‣ Opal: An Operator Algebra View of RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>);
we reproduce an extended version here for completeness, with GKPO deltas and references.</p>
</div>
